# CoralStack Mac mini reconcile config.
#
# install.sh copies this to ~/.coralstack/ollama.env on the box. That copy is
# LOCAL AND UNTRACKED — it holds the push token. Same pattern as the gitignored
# services/*/.env files on the apps VM (see the deploy workflow design note):
# the repo carries the shape, the box carries the secret.

# Uptime Kuma push monitor URL. WITHOUT THIS YOU GET NO ALERTS — the reconcile
# still runs and still exits non-zero, but nothing is listening.
#
# You do NOT create the monitor by hand. It is declared in the repo
# (services/autokuma/monitors/ollama-mac-mini.toml.template) with a token
# pinned by setup.sh, which prints the finished URL as step 6 of its run:
#
#   https://status.<BASE_DOMAIN>/api/push/<OLLAMA_MINI_PUSH_TOKEN>
#
# The PUBLIC status URL, not http://uptime-kuma:3001 — this box isn't on the
# apps VM's docker network, so the container name won't resolve here. If you
# no longer have setup.sh's output, the token is OLLAMA_MINI_PUSH_TOKEN in
# services/autokuma/.env on the apps VM.
#
# The monitor's 48h heartbeat against a daily 06:35 job tolerates one missed
# run; two is a finding. A lapsed heartbeat means the job stopped running at
# all, which is its own alert.
HEALTHCHECK_URL=

# Label in alert text. Only worth changing if a second inference host appears.
OLLAMA_HOST_LABEL=mac-mini

# Overrides — defaults resolve next to the installed script (~/.coralstack/).
# OLLAMA_MODELS_FILE=/Users/you/.coralstack/models.txt
# OLLAMA_VERSIONS_FILE=/Users/you/.coralstack/versions.env

# The Ollama CLI. Auto-detected across /usr/local/bin, Homebrew, and inside the
# app bundle; set explicitly only if yours lives somewhere unusual.
# OLLAMA_BIN=/usr/local/bin/ollama
